e/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136383" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$  the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\n \nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=-3i.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=5\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(-3i)(5) \\\\  & =-15i\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136383" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f29b1fd6ef018996b85e6ba44522fac7df9f0f1f0f46ea4470ac13e4590008ce"} {"question" "q-136383" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136383" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-3i+5j)\\,\\text{cm}"] ["math" "(5i+2j)\\,\\text{cm}"] ["math" "-15i\\,\\text{cm}"] ["math" "-5j\\,\\text{cm}"] ["math" "15j\\,\\text{cm}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136383" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-15i\\,\\text{cm}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-275478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves from the origin with a constant velocity of $(3i-2j)\\,\\text{cm/s}.$ Determine the position vector of the particle$(r)$ after $4$ seconds.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$j)\\text{cm}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-275478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=3i-2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=4\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(3i-2j)(4) \\\\  & =(\\,12\\,i-8\\,j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-275478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f29b1fd6ef018996b85e6ba44522fac7df9f0f1f0f46ea4470ac13e4590008ce"} {"question" "q-275478" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-275478" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-275478" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-275478" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280268" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A skier glides down a smooth slope starting from the origin with a constant velocity of $(6i-1j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Determine the skier's position vector$(r)$ after $5$ seconds.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}  \n$i\\,\\,-$  \n{{field-2}}  \n$j)\\text{m}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280268" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "When a particle (or object) moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector at time $t$ is given by the equation\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position vector.\n\nIn this case, the skier starts at the origin, so\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=6i-1j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the skier after $t=5\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(6i-1j)(5) \\\\  & =(\\,30\\,i-5\\,j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280268" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f29b1fd6ef018996b85e6ba44522fac7df9f0f1f0f46ea4470ac13e4590008ce"} {"question" "q-280268" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280268" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "30"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280268" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280268" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136374" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(2i+3j)\\,\\text{in}$ with a constant velocity of $-j\\,\\text{in/s}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $4$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136374" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$  the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\n \nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=2i+3j,\\,u=-j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=4\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(2i+3j)+(-j)(4) \\\\  & =(2i+3j)-4j \\\\  & =(2i-j)\\,\\text{in}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136374" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f29b1fd6ef018996b85e6ba44522fac7df9f0f1f0f46ea4470ac13e4590008ce"} {"question" "q-136374" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136374" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(2i-j)\\,\\text{in}"] ["math" "(6i+6j)\\,\\text{in}"] ["math" "(8i+11j)\\,\\text{in}"] ["math" "(9i-5j)\\,\\text{in}"] ["math" "-4j\\,\\text{in}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136374" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(2i-j)\\,\\text{in}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136427" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves from the origin with an acceleration of $6i\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $-5j\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $3$ hours." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136427" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=-5j,\\,a=6i.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=3\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(-5j)(3)+\\frac{1}{2}(6i)(3)^{2} \\\\  & =-15j+27i \\\\  & =(27i-15j)\\,\\text{km}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136427" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f29b1fd6ef018996b85e6ba44522fac7df9f0f1f0f46ea4470ac13e4590008ce"} {"question" "q-136427" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136427" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-5i-14j)\\,\\text{km}"] ["math" "(-6i-18j)\\,\\text{km}"] ["math" "(27i-15j)\\,\\text{km}"] ["math" "(7i+10j)\\,\\text{km}"] ["math" "(9i+5j)\\,\\text{km}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136427" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(27i-15j)\\,\\text{km}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves in a uniform gravitational field from the origin with an acceleration of $-10j\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(-i+5j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $3$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=-i+5j,\\,a=-10j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=3\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(-i+5j)(3)+\\frac{1}{2}(-10j)(3)^{2} \\\\  & =(-3i+15j)+9(-5j) \\\\  & =(-3i+15j)-45j \\\\  & =(-3i-30j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/activity-metadata.json" "