ticle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=-2j,\\,u=3i+j,\\,a=4i.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=2\\,\\text{min}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(-2j)+(3i+j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(4i)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =-2j+(6i+2j)+2(4i) \\\\  & =6i+8i \\\\  & =14i\\,\\text{ft}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f29b1fd6ef018996b85e6ba44522fac7df9f0f1f0f46ea4470ac13e4590008ce"} {"question" "q-136416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-7i-14j)\\,\\text{ft}"] ["math" "(15i+5j)\\,\\text{ft}"] ["math" "(5i-j)\\,\\text{ft}"] ["math" "-7j\\,\\text{ft}"] ["math" "14i\\,\\text{ft}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14i\\,\\text{ft}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A parcel robot begins at the position ${r}_{0}=(3i+2j)\\,\\text{cm}$ with an initial velocity of $(i-j)\\,\\text{cm/s}$ and a constant acceleration of $(2i+j)\\,{\\text{cm/s}}^{2}.$ Determine the position vector after $3$ seconds.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$j)\\text{cm}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=3i+2j,\\,u=i-j,\\,a=2i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the parcel robot after $t=3\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(3i+2j)+(i-j)(3)+\\frac{1}{2}(2i+j)(3)^{2} \\\\  & =(3i+2j)+(i-j)(3)+\\frac{1}{2}(18i+9j) \\\\  & =(3i+2j)+(3i-3j)+(9i+4.5j) \\\\  & =(\\,15\\,i+3.5\\,j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f29b1fd6ef018996b85e6ba44522fac7df9f0f1f0f46ea4470ac13e4590008ce"} {"question" "q-280515" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280515" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280515" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280515" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves from the origin with an initial velocity of $(6i+8j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ and experiences a constant acceleration of $(-2i-10j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Determine the position vector of the ball after $1$ second.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$j)\\text{m}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=6i+8j,\\,a=-2i-10j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=1\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(6i+8j)(1)+\\frac{1}{2}(-2i-10j)(1)^{2} \\\\  & =(6i+8j)+\\frac{1}{2}(-2i-10j) \\\\  & =(6i+8j)+(-1i-5j) \\\\  & =(\\,5\\,i+3\\,j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f29b1fd6ef018996b85e6ba44522fac7df9f0f1f0f46ea4470ac13e4590008ce"} {"question" "q-280504" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280504" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280504" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280504" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280537" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A helicopter starts from the position $(5i+2j)\\,\\text{m}$ with an initial velocity of $(-i+3j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ and an acceleration of $(i-j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Find the distance from the helicopter to the origin $(|r|)$ after $2$ seconds.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280537" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=5i+2j,\\,u=-i+3j,\\,a=i-j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the helicopter after $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(5i+2j)+(-i+3j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(i-j)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =(5i+2j)+(-2i+6j)+2(i-j) \\\\  & =(5i+2j)+(-2i+6j)+(2i-2j) \\\\  & =(5i+6j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the helicopter to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|5i+6j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{61} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{61}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280537" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f29b1fd6ef018996b85e6ba44522fac7df9f0f1f0f46ea4470ac13e4590008ce"} {"question" "q-280537" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280537" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{61}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280523" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A weather balloon drifts from the point with position vector $(6i-j)\\,\\text{mi}$ and moves with a constant velocity of $(-3i+2j)\\,\\text{mi/h}.$ Determine the distance $(|r|)$ from the balloon to the origin after $3$ hours.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{mi}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280523" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=6i-j,\\,u=-3i+2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the balloon after $t=3\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(6i-j)+(-3i+2j)(3) \\\\  & =(6i-j)+(-9i+6j) \\\\  & =(-3i+5j)\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the balloon to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|-3i+5j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34}\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280523" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f29b1fd6ef018996b85e6ba44522fac7df9f0f1f0f46ea4470ac13e4590008ce"} {"question" "q-280523" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280523" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{34}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(-i+2j)\\,\\text{km},$ with an acceleration of $(i-j)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $3j\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Find the distance from the particle to the origin after $4$ hours." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=-i+2j,\\,u=3j,\\,a=i-j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=4\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(-i+2j)+(3j)(4)+\\frac{1}{2}(i-j)(4)^{2} \\\\  & =(-i+2j)+(12j)+8(i-j) \\\\  & =(-i+14j)+(8i-8j) \\\\  & =(7i+6j)\\,\\text{km}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the particle to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|7i+6j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{7}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{85}\\,\\text{km}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f29b1fd6ef018996b85e6ba44522fac7df9f0f1f0f46ea4470ac13e4590008ce"} {"question" "q-136438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "13\\,\\text{km}"] ["math" "6\\,\\text{km}"] ["math" "7\\,\\text{km}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{13}\\,\\text{km}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{85}\\,\\text{km}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{85}\\,\\text{km}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves from the origin with a constant velocity of $(i-2j)\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Find the distance from the particle to the origin after $5$ hours." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$  the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=i-2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=5\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(i-2j)(5) \\\\  & =(5i-10j)\\,\\text{km}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the particle to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|5i-10j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-10)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{125} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{km}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f29b1fd6ef018996b85e6ba44522fac7df9f0f1f0f46ea4470ac13e4590008ce"} {"question" "q-136435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "25\\,\\text{km}"] ["math" "5\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{km}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{km}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{15}\\,\\text{km}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{km}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-136435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{km}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A falcon flies from the origin with a constant velocity of $(-6i+8j)\\,\\text{mi/h}.$ Determine the distance $(|r|)$ from the falcon to the origin after $1$ hour.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{mi}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=-6i+8j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the falcon after $t=1\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(-6i+8j)(1) \\\\  & =(-6i+8j)\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the falcon to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|-6i+8j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f29b1fd6ef018996b85e6ba44522fac7df9f0f1f0f46ea4470ac13e4590008ce"} {"question" "q-280528" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "q-280528" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7d6578ca0cf77f2533c987c65115d1809557d05f6c0b9dbda7ad41c7fbb86c4"} {"question" "e-9821" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(3\\mathbf{j} - \\mathbf{i}) \\: \\textrm{mi}$ with a constant velocity of $(\\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j}) \\: \\textrm{mi/h}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $2$ hours." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/example-9821.json" "file_sha256" "f3916ccca6d0c684b1b1fc5c357ff8e6592eacfab4639d807f17cc38e7da8e59"} {"question" "e-9821" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant velocity $\\mathbf{u},$  the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{r}_0 + \\mathbf{u} t,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $\\mathbf{r}_0$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}_0 = 3\\mathbf{j} - \\mathbf{i}, \\qquad \\mathbf u = \\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t = 2 \\: \\textrm{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(3j-i)+(i-j)(2) \\\\  & =(-i+3j)+(2i-2j) \\\\  & =(i+j)\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/example-9821.json" "file_sha256" "f3916ccca6d0c684b1b1fc5c357ff8e6592eacfab4639d807f17cc38e7da8e59"} {"question" "e-9822" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(4\\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j})\\,\\textrm{cm}$ with an acceleration of $(\\mathbf{i} + 3\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{cm/min}^2$ and an initial velocity of $(\\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j}) \\: \\textrm{cm/min}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $4$ minutes." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/example-9822.json" "file_sha256" "f05f3f147ec281dcb8fea7177f5c3f43b4b688c483dd5b41953481b379ec67cd"} {"question" "e-9822" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $\\mathbf{a},$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{r}_0 + \\mathbf{u} t + \\dfrac12 \\mathbf{a} t^2,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $\\mathbf{r}_0$ is the initial position of the particle and $\\mathbf{u}$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}_0 = 4\\mathbf i - \\mathbf j , \\qquad \\mathbf u = \\mathbf{i} +\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad \\mathbf a = \\mathbf{i} + 3\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t = 4 \\, \\textrm{min}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(4i-j)+(i+j)(4)+\\frac{1}{2}(i+3j)(4)^{2} \\\\  & =(4i-j)+(4i+4j)+8(i+3j) \\\\  & =(8i+3j)+(8i+24j) \\\\  & =(16i+27j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/example-9822.json" "file_sha256" "f05f3f147ec281dcb8fea7177f5c3f43b4b688c483dd5b41953481b379ec67cd"} {"question" "e-9824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves from the origin with an acceleration of $(\\mathbf{i} +\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{cm/s}^2$ and an initial velocity of $(-\\mathbf{i}-2\\mathbf{j}) \\: \\textrm{cm/s}.$ Find the distance from the particle to the origin after $6$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/example-9824.json" "file_sha256" "f181e89edb449a760ca06a02fd8fa008c10bccf6ff1e82c979def055fb1bb9ba"} {"question" "e-9824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $\\mathbf{a},$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{r}_0 + \\mathbf{u} t + \\dfrac12 \\mathbf{a} t^2,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $\\mathbf{r}_0$ is the initial position of the particle and $\\mathbf{u}$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}_0 = 0\\mathbf i +0 \\mathbf j , \\qquad \\mathbf u = -\\mathbf{i}-2\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad \\mathbf a = \\mathbf{i} +\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t = 6 \\, \\textrm{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(-i-2j)(6)+\\frac{1}{2}(i+j)(6)^{2} \\\\  & =(-6i-12j)+18(i+j) \\\\  & =(-6i-12j)+(18i+18j) \\\\  & =(12i+6j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the particle to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|12i+6j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{12}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{180} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041674/example-9824.json" "file_sha256" "f181e89edb449a760ca06a02fd8fa008c10bccf6ff1e82c979def055fb1bb9ba"}] "usage" {"q-136416" [] "e-9821" [] "e-9824" [] "e-9822" [] "q-280504" []} "basis" 1621 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186306658 17592186306659 17592186306660 17592186306661 17592186306662 17592186306695 17592186306697] "immutable_fields" [[17592186306657 :answer-field/correct] [17592186306657 :answer-field/id] [17592186306657 :answer-field/key] [17592186306657 :answer-field/type] [17592186306694 :answer-field/correct] [17592186306694 :answer-field/id] [17592186306694 :answer-field/key] [17592186306694 :answer-field/type] [17592186306696 :answer-field/correct] [17592186306696 :answer-field/id] [17592186306696 :answer-field/key] [17592186306696 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
